# Getting Started

Create `.mdx` files under `content/docs` and they become pages.

## Markdown features

Standard Markdown and GFM work out of the box:

- Lists, **bold**, _italic_, and `inline code`
- Tables and task lists
- Syntax-highlighted code blocks
- Headings become the table of contents

```ts
export function hello(name: string): string {
  return `Hello, ${name}!`;
}
```

| Feature | Supported |
|---------|-----------|
| GFM     | yes       |
| TOC     | yes       |

## Blocks

Use GitHub-style callouts:

> [!TIP]
> Callouts are written as `> [!NOTE]`, `> [!TIP]`, `> [!WARNING]`, etc.

